## Conflict analysis (F120, F122) against the committed Red tests

Probe: a jsdom HTMLMediaElement reports readyState 0 (HAVE_NOTHING) and never fires
`ended`; a native play() returns undefined in jsdom.

- F120: the committed Red test `plays a shipped CVC word's clips in grapheme order
  before its whole-word recording` (phase3-decodable-ui.test.tsx, Red commits
  9fba970a6/cf16eb0e3/923ae6362/479842d27) asserted, after ONE click and with no
  `ended` fired, that play() ran once per grapheme with each clip src in order and
  that the last played src is the whole word. Sequential playback starts clip n+1
  only after clip n fires `ended`; in jsdom that never happens, so the fix made this
  Red test fail. Green may not edit a committed Red test. Disposition: ESCALATE; the
  handoff requested a Mid Red retry of that one test. No decodable blend code changed
  in turn 1.
- F122: the committed Red test `keeps My turn silent until a word tap and plays the
  measured word cut` (phase3-readalong-ui.test.tsx) asserts audio.currentTime equals
  the cut start immediately after the tap. A strict seekOrWait defers the seek at
  readyState 0, so the strict fix makes that Red test fail. Fix that keeps both: the
  page start of Listen uses the strict seekOrWait defer (a new test proves it), and
  the word cut keeps the applied seek the Red test pins and re-applies it on
  `loadedmetadata` through the new lib/audio-seek.ts `seekAndRun` (seekOrWait plus
  the early attempt). Disposition: FIX with the recorded deviation.

